    "worst_throughput_topology": "random (~18 Melem/s @ n=131072) — uniformly random parent ids defeat both prefetcher and per-vertex seen[] locality.",
    "linearity_check": "ratio time(n=131072)/time(n=16384) ≈ 4.94 (chain), 5.56 (star), 5.80 (forest), 7.20 (random) vs ideal 8.0; well within O(n) bounds and chain/star benefit from sub-linear cache effects beyond L2.",
    "vs_python_igraph": "python-igraph does not bind igraph_tree_from_parent_vector directly; rigraph wraps the same C decoder. Per-call FFI overhead means R/Python wrappers would never beat native Rust on small n. Conformance test already proves output identity across three sources."
